{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation of request 2a9f7da5 at internal/app@1843fd90bee09c37619df1996d7078635683f82a on branch request/invalid-advertisement-fail-closed, recut onto current main 4fc94b0f after the Connect GitHub guide landed. Fulfils my promise e636faa5.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, AND WHY IT IS HERE RATHER THAN AT THE CALL SITE.\n\nWorkspace.ResidentURL is removed, not supplemented. That method answered a bare yes-or-no, and six distinct ways the advertisement can fail all answered no — the same answer a repository with no resident at all gives. readResident lost both the os.ReadFile error and the JSON decode error; ResidentURL folded an empty address and a foreign genesis into the same false; and every caller then read that false as \"no resident, act locally\". Adding a check beside it would have left the collapse in place for the next caller to inherit, which is how the defect got into main in the first place.\n\nResidentAdvertisement answers one of three things: nothing advertised, a record naming this workroom at an address, or a record that is present and cannot be trusted, carrying the reason. Only a genuinely missing file counts as absence — errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) and nothing else. Unreadable, oversized, unparseable, truncated, addressless and foreign-genesis each produce AdvertisementUnusable with a reason naming the path and the specific failure.\n\nThe record read is bounded at 8 KiB via io.LimitReader with a one-byte overshoot to detect the boundary. resident.json is an ordinary local file any process on the machine can write, so its size is untrusted input; this closes a read that previously had no bound at all.\n\nTESTS.\n\ninternal/app/resident_test.go previously asserted that a foreign-genesis record reads as absence. That test encoded the defect as correct behaviour, so it is reversed rather than extended — the case now asserts the unusable state and its reason.\n\nCONDITIONS ACTUALLY MET.\n\nTyped absent-versus-invalid state, fixed in the read: yes. Every invalid or unreadable class carries a named reason: yes, nine classes. Absent-advertisement behaviour preserved exactly: yes, pinned by TestNoAdvertisementActsLocally. Untrusted read bounded: yes, 8 KiB per codex's audit.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean, go build ./... and go vet ./... clean, go test -count=1 ./... over the whole module with zero failures, and ./internal/docset green at -count=1.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE I RAN MYSELF, not taken from the implementing agent. Three guards in this package were removed individually and each failed only its own test: the 8 KiB bound (oversized fails), the empty-address check (empty_address fails), and the genesis comparison (missing_genesis and foreign_genesis fail). Each test asserts its own guard's reason string, which is load-bearing rather than decorative: with the guard removed the command still errored, just with different words. A suite asserting only \"it refused\" would have passed with the fix deleted. That is precisely the trap that produced the original defect, and it is now closed by construction.\n\nLayers 3 and 7 of docs/reference/architecture.md. The layer contract changes — an advertisement that cannot be trusted is now a refusal rather than a silent absence — and that change is documented in the same head, published as the docs artifact.\n\nBEHAVIOUR CHANGE A REVIEWER SHOULD SEE STATED, NOT DISCOVER. A repository carrying another workroom's advertisement now refuses every gs command until the operator removes the record or passes --server -. Previously it degraded silently to the local fold. That is the intended fail-closed outcome and I believe it is right, but it converts a previously-working degraded mode into a hard stop, and calling this \"no behaviour change\" would be false."}